-- title:
--   Right Λ-ideals of full rank arise from finite ideles
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra, and let $q,q'$ be primes. Assume `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every $v$ in the height one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring (every nonzero element is a unit) exactly when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, finitely generated, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and any order containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $I\subseteq\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule with $z\mu\in I$ for all $z\in I$, $\mu\in\Lambda$, and such that $n\Lambda\subseteq I$ for some nonzero integer $n$. Then there is a unit $x$ of $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^{f}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, where $\mathbb{A}^{f}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $I=\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda\,x$: that is, $I$ consists of exactly those $z\in B$ whose image $z\otimes 1$ lies in $x\cdot\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}\,\Lambda$, the latter being the additive subgroup of $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^{f}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the tensors $\mu\otimes\alpha$ with $\mu\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral.
--
--   This is the idelic form of the local principality of full-rank right ideals of a maximal order in an indefinite rational quaternion algebra ramified exactly at two primes: every such ideal is cut out of $B$ by translating the integral adelic box of $\Lambda$ by a single finite idele. It feeds the description of such ideals as right translates, [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_eq_map_mulRight_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_eq_map_mulRight_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt), in the adelic analysis of the Shimura curves attached to $\Lambda$.
